WEBVTT

00:00.480 --> 00:03.480
<b>Day 81</b>

00:04.370 --> 00:09.990
<i>A few days after our second clash with the 
human army, we were ready for our third.</i>

00:13.670 --> 00:16.250
<i>From around 300 meters away...</i>

00:19.520 --> 00:22.880
<i>I was able to successfully 
snipe someone with a spear.</i>

00:24.610 --> 00:26.440
What just happened?!

00:32.480 --> 00:34.020
Tzenpes.

00:34.450 --> 00:38.200
<i>It produces a limitless number of spears</i>

00:38.200 --> 00:41.400
<i>that can extend as far out as a hundred 
meters from the point of impact.</i>

00:42.990 --> 00:48.830
<i>The battle was over 20 minutes 
after the first strike landed.</i>

00:53.910 --> 00:56.910
Well, that doesn't look very pleasant!

00:56.910 --> 01:01.090
But you sure seem to be having 
a good time, Miss Bloodsato!

01:01.090 --> 01:05.780
Sato's always had a screw loose. 
I wouldn't pay it any mind.

01:06.670 --> 01:09.170
<b>Day 82</b>

01:12.680 --> 01:15.350
<i>And then, the next day...</i>

01:16.030 --> 01:17.920
Those are humans, right?

01:17.920 --> 01:20.180
What're they doing here?

01:22.690 --> 01:24.980
We're attracting a lot of attention.

01:24.980 --> 01:27.940
Should we have come?

01:28.370 --> 01:29.860
Don't worry about it.

01:29.860 --> 01:33.510
The chief here isn't rude like the others.

01:35.060 --> 01:38.230
My apologies for the delay, Lord Ogrou.

03:15.970 --> 03:21.220
Thanks to your exploits, the human 
army has been pushed to the brink.

03:21.550 --> 03:25.940
That said, there's nothing to be gained 
from drawing out this conflict.

03:26.360 --> 03:27.230
Which means?

03:27.940 --> 03:33.700
I would like to send our most 
capable forces into the next battle

03:33.700 --> 03:37.240
to put a decisive end to this war.

03:39.620 --> 03:41.850
If that's what you're paying us to do.

03:43.500 --> 03:47.940
<i>Afterwards, the chief and I went 
over the specifics of our strategy.</i>

03:47.940 --> 03:50.370
<i>Then, on the road back to the village...</i>

03:51.130 --> 03:54.030
Ogrou, I need to make a request.

03:54.030 --> 03:55.760
This is sudden. What's up?

03:56.440 --> 03:59.150
You have my fealty now,

03:59.150 --> 04:03.010
but I ask that you let me fulfill my duty 
as one of the kingdom's knights.

04:03.010 --> 04:06.490
In order to treat the illness 
that plagues our princess...

04:06.490 --> 04:10.650
Would you be willing to send the secret 
elvish medicine to the kingdom?

04:11.650 --> 04:13.650
<i>Getting the kingdom in my debt</i>

04:13.650 --> 04:17.150
<i>would mean having additional 
backup in case of an emergency.</i>

04:17.660 --> 04:19.530
<i>There's one issue, though.</i>

04:20.220 --> 04:23.820
<i>Five great gods are worshiped in this world.</i>

04:23.820 --> 04:26.380
<i>Because their blessings are 
incredibly powerful,</i>

04:26.380 --> 04:30.540
<i>they tend to be the root 
of a lot of religious conflict.</i>

04:30.990 --> 04:36.650
<i>And I happen to have the blessing of the 
God of Demise and Origin.</i>

04:36.650 --> 04:39.490
<i>If someone like me provides the medicine,</i>

04:39.490 --> 04:41.700
<i>it could lead to even more 
trouble down the road.</i>

04:43.210 --> 04:44.810
Wait, hang on...

04:46.450 --> 04:50.640
I'll consider it. I think 
we can make this work.

04:51.320 --> 04:52.870
Thank you, Ogrou!

04:53.810 --> 04:56.320
<b>Day 83</b>

04:57.060 --> 05:00.950
<i>We chose to begin the final battle 
a little bit before dawn.</i>

05:00.950 --> 05:03.870
<i>The enemy's headquarters is 2000 strong,</i>

05:03.870 --> 05:06.420
<i>and has proper security,
 despite the early hour.</i>

05:06.830 --> 05:11.080
<i>Including the 500 elves that
 have joined us, we've got 650.</i>

05:11.080 --> 05:14.210
<i>If we rush in thoughtlessly, we won't win.</i>

05:14.210 --> 05:18.530
<i>Plus, one of my replicants learned 
something interesting yesterday.</i>

05:15.210 --> 05:20.020
Did you hear? They're gonna 
send the Rugald Orden.

05:20.020 --> 05:24.220
Finally! Looks like the elves' 
luck has finally run out.

05:24.220 --> 05:28.720
That's not good news. I didn't think 
they'd bring in the Braves.

05:29.040 --> 05:30.260
Braves?

05:30.740 --> 05:35.720
The Rugald Orden are an order 
of eight heroic warriors.

05:35.720 --> 05:40.260
The ultimate fighting force,
 all eight of them blessed by the gods.

05:41.150 --> 05:44.540
Individually, they're pretty tough,

05:44.540 --> 05:48.250
but they also have the ability to
 empower those who fight at their side.

05:48.740 --> 05:50.000
Which means...

05:50.000 --> 05:53.000
The more allies they have, 
the more dangerous they are.

05:53.000 --> 05:55.440
Well, that's something to look forward to.

05:56.340 --> 05:59.760
<i>I wonder how they're gonna taste.</i>

06:03.730 --> 06:06.760
Okay, it's time for phase one!

06:07.020 --> 06:09.510
Is this really good timing for the skeletons?

06:09.510 --> 06:12.020
It's almost dawn. Are they going to be okay?

06:12.320 --> 06:16.410
Yeah, I made a few special 
tweaks this time around.

06:16.410 --> 06:20.280
Ogrekichi, you guys make sure the enemies 
on the perimeter are taken care of.

06:20.280 --> 06:22.210
Okay. We'll handle it!

06:22.210 --> 06:23.280
What about you, Ogrou?

06:23.280 --> 06:27.150
The skeletons and I are headed 
straight for their center.

06:40.050 --> 06:41.600
Skeletons?!

06:41.600 --> 06:43.550
All of you, engage!

06:48.080 --> 06:49.850
There's so many!

06:50.560 --> 06:53.310
Hold your ground! It won't be long now!

06:59.570 --> 07:03.570
There! They'll be helpless now! 
We'll force them back!

07:08.000 --> 07:09.580
They're not getting any weaker?!

07:09.580 --> 07:13.930
<i>I took my replicants and 
reduced them to a slime form,</i>

07:13.930 --> 07:16.080
<i>before coating the skeletons with them.</i>

07:18.190 --> 07:20.090
What do we do now?!

07:22.870 --> 07:26.640
Any black skeletons still able to move 
should move to back up our people!

07:27.090 --> 07:29.960
I can wrap things up here!

07:34.980 --> 07:39.910
<i>Without this central camp, the enemy's
 command structure will fall apart.</i>

07:42.250 --> 07:44.450
Aw, gimme a break!

07:44.450 --> 07:48.570
Why do I have to go to work 
in a rinky-dink war like this?

07:48.570 --> 07:50.840
We apologize for interrupting your time off.

07:50.840 --> 07:55.630
That said, with your power as a Brave, 
victory will be guaranteed.

07:55.630 --> 07:58.250
Maybe, but wouldn't you have managed anyway

07:58.250 --> 08:01.000
if you all had just fought 
like your lives depended on it?

08:01.000 --> 08:05.770
Sadly, we are not as 
powerful as you are, sir.

08:06.730 --> 08:08.130
I guess it's okay.

08:08.620 --> 08:11.120
This does look pretty interesting, actually.

08:13.810 --> 08:15.640
What is that?! It's coming out of the ground!

08:15.640 --> 08:18.140
He's pulling in the water and blood...

08:25.850 --> 08:27.650
That oughta do it.

08:29.140 --> 08:31.090
Kinda hungry now, though.

08:34.940 --> 08:38.230
Hey! Mister Black Ogre!

08:39.810 --> 08:42.220
Sorry to interrupt your meal.

08:43.420 --> 08:47.920
If you're not busy, how about we fight next?

08:48.520 --> 08:50.430
From the look of you...

08:51.010 --> 08:56.290
I assume you're one of the Rugald Orden, 
Phillippo the Bone Bug Brave.

08:51.970 --> 08:59.940
<b>Phillippo the Bone Bug Brave</b>

08:56.290 --> 08:59.940
Oh, wow! I must be super famous!

09:00.410 --> 09:01.940
I'm not a huge fan of the name, though.

09:01.940 --> 09:06.440
It makes it sound like 
I'm literally a bug, y'know?

09:06.440 --> 09:10.390
I mean, it's an official title and all...

09:10.390 --> 09:14.200
But when someone 
I don't respect uses it,

09:16.160 --> 09:19.710
it really pisses me off. Seriously.

09:20.330 --> 09:25.710
I see. Those compound eyes must be a 
blessing from the God of Demonic Insects.

09:25.710 --> 09:27.960
You know all that, huh?

09:28.290 --> 09:33.970
Wait, are you the one who's been wiping out 
all the soldiers I've sent along so far?!

09:33.970 --> 09:37.470
Dang it! I had my vacation 
canceled because of you!

09:37.470 --> 09:38.720
You big-horned jerk!

09:39.420 --> 09:43.530
<i>He's acting like a brat, but 
this pressure is something else.</i>

09:43.980 --> 09:46.480
<i>He's definitely used to fighting.</i>

09:47.410 --> 09:51.490
So, I'm wondering: You've got a
 divine blessing too, right, Mister Ogre?

09:51.490 --> 09:53.140
Which one?

09:55.490 --> 09:58.740
Aw, not gonna share?

09:59.090 --> 10:00.760
Then I'm wondering...

10:00.760 --> 10:05.950
See, I have these bugs—I call them Undero—
made with a mix of my blessing and necromancy.

10:06.500 --> 10:08.000
I take these...

10:08.000 --> 10:09.760
Do this...

10:13.020 --> 10:14.760
And would you look at that?!

10:14.760 --> 10:17.520
I can make corpses move around!

10:20.240 --> 10:24.900
<i>These aren't zombies. 
The sun's not affecting them.</i>

10:24.900 --> 10:30.400
<i>If I had to guess, those bugs must be
 some kind of parasitic biological weapon.</i>

10:30.400 --> 10:35.460
Now, do you know the difference 
between a Brave, like me, and a Hero?

10:35.830 --> 10:37.650
Something about your individual strengths

10:37.650 --> 10:41.410
and the number of allies 
you can empower, right?

10:41.730 --> 10:43.400
Bingo!

10:43.400 --> 10:46.690
Heroes are more individually powerful,

10:46.690 --> 10:49.670
but can only increase the
 strength of about ten people.

10:49.670 --> 10:53.850
Now, Braves might not be as strong as Heroes,

10:53.850 --> 10:57.320
and we don't make each one of 
our allies quite as strong...

10:57.930 --> 11:03.260
But wait till you see what we can do 
with over a hundred bodies at our disposal!

11:06.560 --> 11:10.070
<i>Did those bugs transform the corpses?!</i>

11:10.070 --> 11:13.170
Now it's time for the fun to begin!

11:13.170 --> 11:16.070
This is my Undero Bazrala: 
Undead Insect Legion!

11:30.670 --> 11:31.920
Whoopsie daisy!

11:37.010 --> 11:39.480
Wow! That's really something, Mister Ogre!

11:39.480 --> 11:43.680
You're able to smash up 
my toys like they're nothing!

11:44.210 --> 11:45.940
In that case, next...

11:47.920 --> 11:50.690
I'm going take direct control!

12:00.310 --> 12:01.620
Wow!

12:01.620 --> 12:05.950
A normal ogre would've been 
dead by now! You really heal fast!

12:05.950 --> 12:08.690
But can you heal from this?!

12:10.460 --> 12:11.640
An earthquake?!

12:23.970 --> 12:25.140
What the...

12:33.570 --> 12:38.240
That's one of my favorite pets! 
His name is Alteilm!

12:38.240 --> 12:42.820
He's pretty famous, too! Got classified 
as a natural disaster and everything!

12:43.240 --> 12:47.400
I normally send him into other
 countries for secret missions, but...

12:47.400 --> 12:51.250
I'm lucky I had called him 
back in for this little outing!

12:53.020 --> 12:57.760
His venom can cause death by organ 
paralysis with the tiniest exposure...

12:58.380 --> 13:02.760
And you're still alive! 
That's so impressive, Mister Ogre!

13:09.890 --> 13:11.020
Ogrou?

13:11.020 --> 13:12.340
What's wrong?!

13:12.770 --> 13:13.910
It's Ogrou!

13:14.400 --> 13:16.800
You got enemies incoming!

13:22.100 --> 13:24.910
Aw, who's a good boy? Nicely done!

13:25.950 --> 13:27.660
I guess we're done here.

13:28.050 --> 13:31.670
You head on back to 
your unfinished job, okay?

13:36.670 --> 13:40.110
Now, then, I bet I can figure 
out what blessing he has

13:40.110 --> 13:43.180
if I take him back and dissect him...

13:43.180 --> 13:46.280
Hey! Anyone alive?

13:46.280 --> 13:47.930
I could use a hand...

13:47.930 --> 13:49.420
Huh?

14:03.110 --> 14:05.910
Well, you really got me there, Mister Ogre!

14:06.390 --> 14:09.160
How the heck did you survive all that?

14:09.160 --> 14:11.450
Why would I tell you?

14:11.450 --> 14:13.160
That's fair!

14:13.450 --> 14:17.000
Most likely, it was just a fake corpse.

14:17.490 --> 14:21.420
But if I didn't notice,
it was a really good fake!

14:21.820 --> 14:25.160
And Alteilm is already pretty far away...

14:25.700 --> 14:30.180
Oh, well. Time for my first secret weapon!

14:30.650 --> 14:35.150
But first, how about we do 
proper introductions?

14:35.150 --> 14:39.190
Hell no. I'd rather nobody 
know who I am just yet.

14:40.610 --> 14:42.970
That's just cold, Mister Ogre!

14:42.970 --> 14:45.700
Fine then! I can still 
introduce myself, at least!

14:46.020 --> 14:49.180
My name is Phillippo Berd Lokkarta.

14:49.180 --> 14:52.590
I'm ranked seventh 
in the country, by the way!

14:52.590 --> 14:55.080
You're about as strong as me, 
so I'd wager that makes you—

14:55.080 --> 14:56.210
Yikes!

14:59.430 --> 15:02.460
I wasn't finished yet! 
You're such a meanie, Mister Ogre!

15:14.980 --> 15:20.370
Wow, you forced me to use the second secret
weapon before I could finish using the first one!

15:20.370 --> 15:21.480
Not that it matters.

15:29.990 --> 15:33.870
Okay, now you're starting to smell delicious.

15:33.870 --> 15:35.750
And any good meal takes effort!

15:37.270 --> 15:41.250
Feeling nice and motivated, huh? 
It's too late, though!

15:52.620 --> 15:55.830
I can't believe you're able to 
dodge that and fight back!

15:55.830 --> 15:57.980
You're just full of surprises, Mister Ogre!

15:58.290 --> 16:02.810
All this and you haven't even 
undergone an Epic Awakening, huh?

16:02.810 --> 16:03.980
That's so weird!

16:04.470 --> 16:06.340
Epic Awakening?

16:07.800 --> 16:09.780
You look like you wanna ask,
 "What the heck is that?!"

16:09.780 --> 16:14.260
But since you ignored me a bunch, 
I'm not telling! Serves you right!

16:14.990 --> 16:17.250
I can always force you to talk.

16:17.250 --> 16:18.940
You sure about that?

16:18.940 --> 16:24.000
Hey, would you mind if 
I put on my insect outfit, too?

16:25.030 --> 16:27.010
Don't be silly... You can't possibly—

16:28.510 --> 16:30.510
Exoskeleton!

16:37.890 --> 16:39.950
Grow Elytron!

16:40.900 --> 16:45.650
Wow! That's amazing! 
You never run out of tricks, huh?!

16:45.650 --> 16:48.530
Looks like we match, now!

17:11.670 --> 17:14.430
That oughta take care of
 the enemies around here.

17:15.860 --> 17:17.410
What's wrong, Dhami?

17:17.410 --> 17:19.430
I have a really bad feeling!

17:19.430 --> 17:21.080
What for?

17:23.120 --> 17:25.300
Well, this has been a blast!

17:25.300 --> 17:27.940
I figure this is a good time to stop, though.

17:28.330 --> 17:30.450
You seriously think I'm letting you go?

17:30.450 --> 17:34.200
Nope, but I'm still gonna get away!

17:38.200 --> 17:39.880
Whoop!

17:41.210 --> 17:44.210
I'm a pretty fast runner, after all!

17:44.210 --> 17:45.710
Get back here!

17:46.710 --> 17:48.460
That thing can move even when he's gone?!

17:50.090 --> 17:51.520
Out of the way!

17:53.730 --> 17:58.350
Fair enough. He really can run fast.

18:02.350 --> 18:07.010
<i>The Bone Bug Brave, Phillippo... 
I'll eat you soon enough.</i>

18:07.010 --> 18:08.730
Ogrou!

18:13.020 --> 18:14.170
You okay?

18:14.170 --> 18:16.060
Somehow, yeah.

18:17.410 --> 18:19.690
Ugh, what are those?! Nasty!

18:19.690 --> 18:20.870
Well...

18:21.200 --> 18:23.790
Let's see how things are going on his end.

18:25.290 --> 18:27.430
<i>As I was fighting Phillippo,</i>

18:27.430 --> 18:30.380
<i>I used a replicant that I created 
with some stealth abilities...</i>

18:30.380 --> 18:34.010
Our forces have essentially 
been wiped out...

18:30.730 --> 18:33.350
<i>and had it run deep into the woods.</i>

18:34.010 --> 18:36.710
Impossible! At the hands of the elves?!

18:35.190 --> 18:36.710
Don't move, just listen.

18:36.710 --> 18:42.130
No, they were apparently faced 
with an army of skeletons...

18:37.900 --> 18:43.280
You're the next king of this country and
 commander of its royal armed forces.

18:43.860 --> 18:46.920
We have no desire to continue this war.

18:47.760 --> 18:49.790
Wh-Who are you?

18:49.790 --> 18:52.400
Check inside your armor.

18:57.000 --> 18:58.380
When did you...

18:58.690 --> 19:03.410
It's what you people need more than 
anything else at the moment.

19:03.810 --> 19:08.170
Take it to your sick princess at once.

19:08.890 --> 19:11.650
Is this the secret elvish medicine?!

19:11.650 --> 19:16.880
Now that you have it, your men 
won't have to keep dying for nothing.

19:17.680 --> 19:20.010
I bid you farewell.

19:26.130 --> 19:27.250
Your Highness?

19:27.250 --> 19:30.190
You don't look well. Is something the matter?

19:30.190 --> 19:31.720
No, it's fine...

19:32.160 --> 19:33.450
Send a messenger!

19:33.450 --> 19:34.290
Where to?

19:34.290 --> 19:37.610
To our homeland! Let them know 
we have the elvish medicine!

19:40.990 --> 19:43.670
<i>If I had killed the future king right there,</i>

19:43.670 --> 19:47.140
<i>the kingdom would've put everything 
they had into wiping the elves out.</i>

19:47.610 --> 19:50.710
<i>An all-out war like that should be avoided.</i>

19:51.200 --> 19:53.460
Alright, here goes!

19:56.970 --> 20:00.500
Good! That'll work as a defensive wall.

20:00.500 --> 20:03.060
Let's move the injured 
out of here while we can.

20:03.060 --> 20:04.470
Got it.

20:05.630 --> 20:10.570
<i>Our people. This forest. Our village.</i>

20:10.980 --> 20:14.030
<i>And our ally, the Chief of the Elves...</i>

20:14.360 --> 20:16.790
<i>We can't afford to lose any of them.</i>

20:19.970 --> 20:21.120
Are you okay?

20:21.120 --> 20:23.740
We need to hurry... rendezvous 
with the main force...

20:26.250 --> 20:27.540
Go on.

20:28.610 --> 20:33.120
The battle's over. No one else needs to die.

20:36.770 --> 20:43.010
<i>That's right. With the fighting over, 
there's something that needs to be done.</i>

20:44.020 --> 20:47.740
<i>Six hobgoblins, two hobgoblin mages...</i>

20:47.740 --> 20:50.680
<i>eight goblins, ten kobolds,</i>

20:50.680 --> 20:54.530
<i>four male elves. A total of 30.</i>

20:54.530 --> 20:57.730
<i>All killed in action as part of our 
mercenary company, Parabellum.</i>

20:58.850 --> 20:59.960
Ogrou...

21:04.290 --> 21:07.990
<i>In this world, the dead need 
to be put to rest properly,</i>

21:07.990 --> 21:10.290
<i>or you risk them coming 
back as zombies or ghosts.</i>

21:10.750 --> 21:13.880
<i>So after offering some prayers, 
they were cremated.</i>

21:14.290 --> 21:16.590
Rest in peace, everyone...

21:17.090 --> 21:20.300
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry!

21:20.300 --> 21:22.080
You guys can rest easy.

21:23.300 --> 21:27.170
Brave warriors all, 
who fought to the very end.

21:27.170 --> 21:32.310
Your valor has forever 
been burned into my sight.

21:32.310 --> 21:35.690
Maybe if I had been more powerful...

21:36.780 --> 21:42.300
<i>Everyone reacted in different ways, 
but I didn't feel particularly sad.</i>

21:42.770 --> 21:47.080
<i>There was no cause for tears or regrets.</i>

21:50.850 --> 21:55.230
<i>But... I did feel the need to 
cling to life as hard as I could,</i>

21:55.830 --> 21:58.160
<i>because they couldn't anymore.</i>

23:29.970 --> 23:39.980
<b>Next Time:</b>
